  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Sunday) \nIssued at 1033 PM CST Sun Nov 1 2026\n\nWeak ridging will build in behind the trough as it departs on \nTuesday. This will usher in cooler, dry air in behind it and highs \nwill be slightly below normal in the low-to-mid 60s on the Caprock \nand near 70 off the Caprock. Wednesday will be a few degrees warmer \nin a more zonal flow pattern aloft. Another fast moving upper low \nwill move over our area on Thursday. The latest ECMWF shows some \nprecipitation clipping the far southeastern Panhandle, however \nuncertainty remains and it does not look to be anything significant \nat this time. Otherwise cooler and dry conditions will round out the \nwork week.",
